@host = http://localhost:5080

### Where to start — lists every route, plus the Swagger and OpenAPI links.
GET {{host}}/

### Health: confirms which provider the Unit of Work actually resolved.
GET {{host}}/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Patients — run this FIRST: you need an id to POST a claim against.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name patients
GET {{host}}/api/patients

### Filter by name (PatientDirectorySpec, not a leaked IQueryable).
GET {{host}}/api/patients?name=a

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Claims
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Search. Every filter is optional — this is ClaimSearchSpec doing the work.
GET {{host}}/api/claims?page=1&pageSize=10

### Narrow it: payer + status + number prefix.
GET {{host}}/api/claims?payer=PBM-01&status=Submitted&number=CLM

### Projection — six columns per row, never a whole aggregate.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/summaries?payer=PBM-01

### The named business rule: unsettled for thirty days or more.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/outstanding/PBM-01

### Soft-deleted claims — the global query filter, opted out of.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/deleted

### Submit a claim. PatientId is taken from the /api/patients call above, so run
### that one first; Number must be unique or you get a 409.
# @name created
POST {{host}}/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patients.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "number": "CLM-9001",
  "serviceDate": "2026-09-01",
  "payerCode": "PBM-01",
  "lines": [
    { "procedureCode": "99213", "quantity": 1 },
    { "procedureCode": "85025", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### Read it back with its lines and patient in one round trip.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/{{created.response.body.id}}

### Re-price through a Strategy picked at run time. See /api/pricing/plans for the list.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{created.response.body.id}}/reprice?planType=Standard

### Mark paid — raises ClaimPaid, dispatched after the commit, visible in /api/audit.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{created.response.body.id}}/pay

### Delete — the Unit of Work turns this into a soft delete.
DELETE {{host}}/api/claims/{{created.response.body.id}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Reports and diagnostics
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### NOTE: currently returns 500 — EF cannot aggregate over the owned Money type.
GET {{host}}/api/reports/totals-by-payer?from=2025-01-01&to=2026-12-31

### What the domain-event observers have recorded since startup.
GET {{host}}/api/audit

### The Strategy registry — each plan is a separate IPricingRule.
GET {{host}}/api/pricing/plans

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Pattern catalogue
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Every demo in the catalogue.
GET {{host}}/api/patterns

### One of them.
GET {{host}}/api/patterns/strategy

### Run it and see its output.
POST {{host}}/api/patterns/strategy/run
